| — |\n| 4 | 0.95 | 0.96 | about 150 worse (more shortages) |\n| 5 | ≈1.10 | ≈1.24 | about 1,500 worse (storage and unsold stock) |\n| 6 | ≈1.15 | ≈1.16 | worse |\n| 1 | 1.00 | ≈1.35 | much worse on product 1 |\n| 2 | ≈1.31 | ≈1.32 | worst of the daily plans |\n\n**Plans that skip days**\n- **Candidate 3** orders every 2 days. That saves 14 order fees of 47 (about 658). But one day's goods sit in storage an extra night, costing about 630. That nets out to about zero. Its multiples (≈1.1 and ≈1.2) then put it about 1,400 behind candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 7** orders every 3 days. The extra storage (about 45 per day) costs more than the fees it saves (about 31 per day). It also risks going over the 288-unit capacity around days 14–17.\n\n**Uncertainty**\nCandidate 0 keeps stock low, so a run of high demand mostly causes shortages, not big write-offs. My shortfall figures are rough. Candidates 0 and 4 are close, but candidate 0 still leads after allowing for that."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3836, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3836}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T19:30:26.512Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPWQ91fBDcxU3qfzzHLV"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XNXpXp8H7F4qjhppDcRkV6", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgPWQ9EoPhTc9cbF