d saves about 134 on holding, net ≈ −120 versus Candidate 0.\n- **Item 1.** Over days 4–29, expected demand is ≈956 units, spread about ±62.\n  - Candidate 0 orders 914. Expected lost sales ≈74, leftover ≈32.\n  - Candidates 3 and 7 order 1078. They gain about 58 sales, which almost exactly offsets the extra purchases. However, the leftover grows to about 138 by the end, so holding costs about 640 more.\n  - Candidates 5, 1, 6 and 2 order 1.16–1.36× the forecast for item 1, which is even worse.\n  - Candidate 4 orders about 873. It loses about 230 versus Candidate 0.\n- **Ordering less often.**\n  - Candidate 3 (every 2 days) saves about 658 in per-order fees. It spends about 580 holding the second day's stock overnight, so it nets only ≈ +80.\n  - Candidate 7 (every 3 days) spends about 133 more on holding per cycle while saving 94 in fees, so it comes out behind.\n\n**Ranking versus Candidate 0 (approximate)**\n\n| Candidate | Difference |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | best |\n| 4 | ≈ −350 |\n| 3 | ≈ −1000 |\n| 7 | ≈ −1150 |\n| 5, 6, 1, 2 | worse still |\n\nCandidates 3, 5, 6 and 7 also overflow the 288-unit warehouse near the end; this makes little difference because the lost units would have gone unsold anyway.\n\nAll plans face the same random demand, so their results move together. The main risk is that demand runs high, in which case Candidate 0's shortages would cost more than I estimated."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3882, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3882}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T19:31:44.449Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPWURfdMf5Y7HWFRgh6N"}, {"type": "stream_event",